      "text": "## The Big Picture: Where, Not Just What"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md#002",
      "path": [
        "07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-vision:07-detection-and-tracking, git-history:computer-vision:07-detection-and-tracking]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md",
        "concepts": "[object detection, R-CNN, YOLO, non-maximum suppression, IoU, mAP, Kalman filter, optical flow, tracking]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:detection-and-tracking",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[object detection]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Detection and Tracking",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Classification (guide 05) answers *what* is in an image. Detection answers *what and\nwhere* — it returns a box and a label per object. Tracking extends detection through\ntime — it follows each object across video frames, maintaining identity. This guide\ncovers the two detector families (region-based R-CNN and single-shot YOLO), the metrics\nthat govern them (IoU, mAP), the cleanup step (NMS), and the temporal machinery (Kalman\nfiltering, optical flow, multi-object tracking)."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md#003",
      "path": [
        "07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-vision:07-detection-and-tracking, git-history:computer-vision:07-detection-and-tracking]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-vision/07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md",
        "concepts": "[object detection, R-CNN, YOLO, non-maximum suppression, IoU, mAP, Kalman filter, optical flow, tracking]",
        "current_path": "computer-vision/07-DETECTION-AND-TRACKING.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-vision:detection-and-tracking",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-vision",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[object detection]",
        "section": "computing-software",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Detection and Tracking",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              CLASSIFY -> DETECT -> TRACK  (adding location, then time)       |\n|                                                                              |\n|  CLASSIFY            DETECT                    TRACK                         |\n|  \"cat\"              \"cat @ box1, 0.9\"         \"cat#3 @ box1 -> box1' -> ...\" |\n|                     \"dog @ box2, 0.8\"          maintain IDENTITY over frames |\n|                                                                              |\n|  .-------.          .-------.                  frame t      frame t+1        |\n|  | whole |          | [box] |                  .--[#3]--.   .---[#3]-.       |\n|  | image |          |  [box]|                  |        |   |        |       |\n|  '-------'          '-------'                  '--------'   '--------'       |\n|   one label         many boxes + labels        boxes LINKED across time      |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
